ajit supplementation. J Int Soc Sports Nutr. 2019;16(1):1-9. doi:10.1186/s12970-019-0270-2.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">8. Jäger R, Purpura M, Kingsley M, Wilde P, Cohen J, Maixner W, et al. The use of shilajit as a dietary supplement: A systematic review. J Int Soc Sports Nutr. 2016;13:24. doi:10.1186/s12970-016-0139-5.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">9. Lee MS, Yang EJ, Kim JI, Ernst E. Ginseng for cognitive function in Alzheimer's disease: A systematic review. Clin Psychopharmacol Neurosci. 2016 Aug;14(3):181-92. doi:10.1111/cpr.12696.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">10. Cho WC, Leung KN. In vitro and in vivo anti-tumor effects of Astragalus membranaceus. Cancer Lett. 2007 Apr 8;252(1):43-54. doi:10.1016/j.canlet.2006.12.030.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">11. Villarreal DT. What are the health benefits of ginseng? Medical News Today. [Internet]. Available from: https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/262982.</span></p>",
        "ggwRLxP0iIL_text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">12. Gunnars K. 7 proven health benefits of ginseng. Healthline. [Internet]. Available from: https://www.healthline.com/nutrition/ginseng-benefits.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">13. Panossian A, Wikman G. Effects of adaptogens on the central nervous system and the molecular mechanisms associated with their stress-protective activity. Pharmaceuticals (Basel). 2010 Mar;3(1):188-224. doi:10.3390/ph3010188.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">14. Leonard J. The smart girl’s guide to adaptogens. Healthline. [Internet]. Available from: https://www.healthline.com/health/stress/smart-girls-guide-to-adaptogens.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">15. Reid Health. Adaptogens: 5 stress management plants. [Internet]. Available from: https://www.reidhealth.org/blog/adaptogens-5-stress-management-plants.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">16. Cleveland Clinic. Benefits of holy basil for your body and mind. [Internet]. Available from: https://health.clevelandclinic.org/benefits-of-holy-basil.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">17. UCLA Health. What are adaptogens and should you be taking them? [Internet]. Available from: https://www.uclahealth.org/news/article/what-are-adaptogens-and-should-you-be-taking-them.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">18. Lee MS, Yang EJ, Kim JI, Ernst E. Ginseng for cognitive function in Alzheimer's disease: A systematic review. Clin Psychopharmacol Neurosci. 2016 Aug;14(3):181-92. doi:10.1111/cpr.12696.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">19. Gunnars K. Caffeine 101: what it is and how it works. Healthline. [Internet]. Available from: https://www.healthline.com/nutrition/what-is-caffeine.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">20. Villarreal DT. Everything you need to know about caffeine. Medical News Today. [Internet]. Available from: https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/285194.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">21. NIVEA. Caffeine for your skin: what it does and how it works. [Internet]. Available from: https://www.nivea.co.uk/advice/skin/caffeine-for-skin.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">22. Hale Cosmeceuticals. Unveiling the wonders of Japanese peppermint oil. [Internet]. Available from: https://www.halecosmeceuticals.com/blog/unveiling-the-wonders-of-japanese-peppermint-oil.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">23. McKay DL, Blumberg JB. A review of the bioactivity and potential health benefits of peppermint tea (Mentha piperita L.). Phytother Res. 2006 Aug;20(8):619-33. doi:10.1002/ptr.1936.</span><br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">24. WebMD. Japanese mint: Uses, side effects, interactions, dosage, and warning. [Internet]. Available from: https://www.webmd.com/vitamins/ai/ingredientmono-616/japanese-mint.</span></p>"
